  "docs/edit-semantics.md"
 ],
 "notes": "An implicit key is a single line of at most 1024 characters (section 7.4.2), so `<1100 k>: 2` would not read back as a key. The explicit form, `? key` then `: value`, has no such limit, and the key text is written plain like the sibling key. It is the layout that keeps the document valid and exact without touching `a: 1`. The added key is 1100 characters (the letter k).",
 "provenance": {
  "reference": "A writer that added a key of 1100 characters as an implicit key, which the document then could not be read back."
 },
